Ethics, value, and moral reasoning (@ethics-value-and-moral-reasoning: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_5M0CC0HK1Q4GDME0G52DEEBR7X
Ethics asks how people should act, what makes a life good, and how obligations or values can be justified. This material connects virtue, duty, consequences, care, character, moral disagreement, and metaethical questions about the meaning and basis of moral claims. Develop arguments through cases and objections, distinguishing what happens from what ought to happen. Link professional and research ethics, collective decisions, personal action, and literary depictions of moral life through the same concepts where appropriate.

**Parent:** [Philosophy](../Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).
